<title>USA: Howell Corp Q1 net and share rise.</title>
<headline>Howell Corp Q1 net and share rise.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>QUARTER ENDED</p>
<p>								  MARCH 31,</p>
<p>							    1997	 1996</p>
<p>			   (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>STATEMENT OF EARNINGS</p>
<p> Revenues						17,645   166,257</p>
<p> Product costs and expenses			15,348   162,488</p>
<p> Other expense					    144     1,928</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes		     2,153     1,841</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			   751	 646</p>
<p> Net earnings					   1,402     1,195</p>
<p> Preferred dividends				    604	 604</p>
<p> Earnings on common stock			     798	 591</p>
<p> Earnings per common share			    .16	 .12</p>
<p> Wtd. avg. common shares outstanding	    4,985     4,934</p>
<p> Preferred shares outstanding			 690	 690</p>
<p>Cash flow (net earnings plus non-cash items)</p>
<p>							    4,209     5,896</p>
<p>NOTES: Lower 1997 revenue was due to Q4 1996 sale of two corporate subsidiaries engaged in crude oil gathering, marketing, and transportation.  Increased earnings at Howell Petroleum and Howell Hydrocarbons &amp; Chemicals more than offset the reduced earnings due to the sale of these downstream assets.</p>
</text>
